For me, there's nothing to break me out of carelessness like "You die! But
wait..." Maybe that doesn't work for you, in which I guess the amulet is
less helpful... but I still have never seen any real (not constructed
for example) situation in which an amulet of ESP would have trumped an
amulet of lifesaving. Obviously if you keep wearing ESP and keep winning
then by all means continue. But to me, the only time I really want to
know what's where on the map in the lategame (when I have a choice of
amulets) is on Astral, and once I know where the Riders and Archons are,
I'm pretty much set. I can do this with a blindfold, and half the time
the priests are going to grow scales over my eyes anyway. So I get the
information I need without ESP. I generally don't need lifesaving either,
but it protects me against all sorts of stupid slipups on a tactical
level, where ESP only helps me on a strategic level. In a guaranteed
80x20 map with only a few points of difference each time you get there
that can be beated in fourteen turns, I'll take the tactical advantage.

